{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jer-2-1","title":"Jeremiah 2:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 God having shewed his former kindness, expostulates with the Jews on their causeless and unexampled revolt. 14 They are the causes of their own calamities. 18 The sins and idolatries of Judah. 35 Her confidence is rejected.</p>\n<p>the word. 1:11; 7:1; 23:28; Eze 7:1; Heb 1:1; 2Pe 1:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-2-2","title":"Jeremiah 2:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>cry. 7:2; 11:6; 19:2; Pr 1:20; 8:1-4; Isa 58:1; Ho 8:1; Jon 1:2; Mt 11:15 Lu 12:13 thee. or, for thy sake. the kindness. Ex 14:31; 15:1-20; Eze 16:8,22,60; 23:3,8,19; Ho 2:15 thine espousals. Ex 24:3-8; So 3:11; Ex 16:8 when. 6; De 2:7; 8:2,15,16; Ne 9:12-21; Isa 63:7-14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-2-3","title":"Jeremiah 2:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>holiness. Ex 19:5,6; De 7:6; 14:2; 26:19; Zec 14:20,21; Eph 1:4; 1Pe 2:9 the first-fruits. Ex 22:29; 23:16; Nu 18:12; Am 6:1; *marg: Ro 11:16; 16:5; Jas 1:18; Re 14:4 all that. 12:14; 50:7; Ex 4:22,23; Ps 81:14,15; 105:14,15,25-36; Isa 41:11 Isa 47:6; Joe 1:3,7,8; Zec 1:15; 2:8; 12:2-4; Ac 9:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-2-4","title":"Jeremiah 2:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Hear ye. 5:21; 7:2; 13:15; 19:3; 34:4; 44:24-26; Isa 51:1-4; Ho 4:1; Mic 6:1 all the families. 31:1; 33:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-2-5","title":"Jeremiah 2:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>What. 31; Isa 5:3,4; 43:22,23; Mic 6:2,3 are gone. 12:2; Isa 29:13; Eze 11:15; Mt 15:8 walked. 10:8,14,15; 14:22; 